---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Davis Weather Station collects, uses, shares, and protects personal information."
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Davis Weather Station (“we”, “us”, “our”) operates <strong>davisweatherstation.com</strong>, an independent
    directory of authorized Davis Instruments resellers, product information, and a smart buying guide. For the
    purposes of applicable data-protection law, we act as the controller of the personal information described in
    this policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    This Site is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Davis Instruments. We do not sell products.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Scope of this policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy applies to personal information we collect through the Site, including the quote form. It does not
    apply to reseller websites or services. Once your information is sent to a reseller, the reseller’s own privacy
    policy applies to their handling of it.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Information you provide</h2>
  <p>When you use the Smart Buying Guide quote form, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name and email address.</li>
    <li>The subject and message you submit.</li>
    <li>The country and reseller you select.</li>
    <li>The products, tiers, and configuration generated by the guide.</li>
    <li>The date and time of your submission.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please do not include payment-card details, passwords, government identifiers, health information, or other
    sensitive information in the message field.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you subscribe to the newsletter, we collect your email address and the date you subscribed so we can send
    occasional weather-station tips and updates. You can ask us to remove your address at any time through the
    contact page.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>When you visit the Site or submit the form, we may collect limited technical information:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The country associated with your connection (derived from request headers).</li>
    <li>Your browser user agent.</li>
    <li>A one-way hash of your IP address, used only for rate limiting and abuse prevention.</li>
    <li>The date and time of your request and basic security signals.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not store your raw IP address in the quote database. We do not use advertising trackers or third-party
    analytics scripts. We record only aggregate page-view counts for each page; those counts do not include your name,
    email address, or quote content and are not linked to your submission.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    The Site uses only strictly necessary cookies and similar storage, primarily for security and bot protection
    through a bot-protection service. See our <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To deliver your quote request to the reseller you selected.</li>
    <li>To keep a record of requests so we can follow up, resend, or investigate delivery failures.</li>
    <li>To detect, prevent, and investigate spam, abuse, fraud, and automated submissions.</li>
    <li>To operate, maintain, troubleshoot, and improve the Site.</li>
    <li>To respond to your questions and requests.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies, we rely on the following legal bases:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> — when you submit the quote form and agree to this policy.</li>
    <li><strong>Steps at your request before entering a contract</strong> — delivering your request to a reseller.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — operating the Site, preventing abuse, and maintaining records, balanced against your rights.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — when we must retain or disclose information by law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. How we share information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The selected reseller</strong> receives your name, email, message, country, and configuration so they can respond with a quote.</li>
    <li><strong>Our service providers</strong> provide hosting, database, email delivery, security, and bot protection.</li>
    <li><strong>Professional advisers and authorities</strong> may receive information where required by law or necessary to protect rights and safety.</li>
    <li><strong>Business transfers</strong> — information may be transferred as part of a merger, acquisition, or sale of the Site, subject to this policy.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information. We do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising. See our{' '}
    <a href="/do-not-sell/">Do Not Sell or Share</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>9. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Our service providers, may process information in countries other than your own. Where
    required, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as standard contractual clauses or equivalent mechanisms. Data
    protection laws in those countries may differ from those in your jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Quote requests are retained for as long as needed to handle your inquiry, maintain business records, resolve
    disputes, and prevent abuse. We may retain a minimal record of a request after deletion for legal, security, or
    backup purposes. When information is no longer needed, we delete or anonymise it.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable technical and organisational measures, including server-side validation, bot-protection checks,
    rate limiting, access controls, and encrypted transport. No method of transmission or storage is completely
    secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on your location, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access the personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li>Correct inaccurate information.</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your information.</li>
    <li>Restrict or object to certain processing.</li>
    <li>Receive a portable copy of information you provided.</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
    <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data-protection authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise a right, contact us through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or email{' '}
    <a href="mailto:contact@davisweatherstation.com">contact@davisweatherstation.com</a>. We may need to verify your
    identity before acting on a request.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is not directed to children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.
    If you believe a child has submitted information, contact us and we will take appropriate steps to delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Do Not Sell or Share</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information or share it for cross-context behavioural advertising. For California
    residents, see our <a href="/do-not-sell/">Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top of this page shows the latest
    revision. Material changes will be reflected on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions or requests:{' '}
    <a href="mailto:contact@davisweatherstation.com">contact@davisweatherstation.com</a> or the{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
